</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the mean of quartic forms comes from <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathbf{x}}{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{x}}{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}]={\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{A}}+{\mathbf{A}}^{\top}){\mathbf{\Sigma}}+\tr({\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathbf{x}}{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{x}}{\mathbf{x}}^{\top}]={\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{A}}+{\mathbf{A}}^{\top}){\mathbf{\Sigma}}+\tr({\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> for an arbitrary matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, see Sec.8.2.4. in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Petersen et al. (2008)</a></cite>. Moreover, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
