<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+2{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}\Big(2(n+2)\cdot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}+(n+2)\cdot\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}\Big){\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}-(n+2)\cdot({\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+2{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}\Big(2(n+2)\cdot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}+(n+2)\cdot\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}\Big){\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}-(n+2)\cdot({\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(266)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E267"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-(n+2)\left(q^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+2q\cdot\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+4q\cdot{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-(n+2)\left(q^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+2q\cdot\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+4q\cdot{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(267)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E268"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+2{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\left(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+q^{2}\right)\cdot\sigma^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐀𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+2{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\left(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+q^{2}\right)\cdot\sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(268)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as in Eq. <a href="#A1.E250" title="Equation 250 ‣ Theorem A.13. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">250</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite, it follows that <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also positive definite and hence invertible.
Thus, we can rewrite the above expression as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E269"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+2{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\left(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+q^{2}\right)\cdot\sigma^{2}=-\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)+c," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐀𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}{\mathbf{v}}_{21}+2{\mathbf{v}}_{21}^{\top}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\left(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+q^{2}\right)\cdot\sigma^{2}=-\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)+c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(269)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}\left({\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}+{\mathbf{C}}\right){\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\left(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+q^{2}\right)\cdot\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐁𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}\left({\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}+{\mathbf{C}}\right){\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\left(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+q^{2}\right)\cdot\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the condition in (<a href="#A1.E248" title="Equation 248 ‣ Theorem A.13. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">248</span></a>) is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E270"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)\leq c." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)^{\top}{\mathbf{A}}\left({\mathbf{v}}_{21}-{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)\leq c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(270)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.14</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Test Error of Pretrained Models)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameters in (<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Corollary 4.1 (Optimal Parameters of Pretrained Models; Corollary of Theorem 1 in ( ) ). ‣ 4.1 Pretraining ‣ 4 Optimal Parameters and Test Error of Learned Linear Attention Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) which minimize the loss <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Evaluation Metric and Training Objective. ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Then, for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E271"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E271.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}=\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}},\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};0,{\mathbf{\theta}})\geq\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}},\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};n,{\mathbf{\theta}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}=\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}},\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};0,{\mathbf{\theta}})\geq\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}},\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};n,{\mathbf{\theta}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(271)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E272"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E272.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}\cdot\frac{\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}}{a_{d}(2-a_{d})\cdot\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}}-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}\cdot\frac{\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}}{a_{d}(2-a_{d})\cdot\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}}-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E272.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\text{ where }a_{i}:=\frac{m\lambda_{i}}{(m+1)\lambda_{i}+\tr({\mathbf{\Sigma}})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\text{ where }a_{i}:=\frac{m\lambda_{i}}{(m+1)\lambda_{i}+\tr({\mathbf{\Sigma}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(272)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-shot error is monotone decreasing in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus the minimum error is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E273"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E273.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}},\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};n,{\mathbf{\theta}})=\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-1)^{2}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}},\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};n,{\mathbf{\theta}})=\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-1)^{2}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(273)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which converges to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">From (<a href="#A1.E206" title="Equation 206 ‣ Corollary A.7 (Optimal Parameters of Pretrained Models; Corollary of Theorem 1 in ( ) ). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">206</span></a>), which gives <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{v}}_{21}={\mathbf{0}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{v}}_{21}={\mathbf{0}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the condition (<a href="#A1.E249" title="Equation 249 ‣ Theorem A.13. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">249</span></a>) in Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem A.13. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a> simplifies to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E274"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}\geq{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}\left({\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}+{\mathbf{C}}\right){\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐁𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐁𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{\theta}}\geq{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}\left({\mathbf{B}}{\mathbf{A}}^{-1}{\mathbf{B}}+{\mathbf{C}}\right){\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(274)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem A.13. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>, (<a href="#A1.E271" title="Equation 271 ‣ Corollary A.14 (Test Error of Pretrained Models). ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">271</span></a>) holds if and only if <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{D}}:={\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{D}}:={\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E275"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E275.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E275.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(n+1)\cdot\Big({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}-2\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(n+1)\cdot\Big({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}-2\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(275)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E276"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E276.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-(n+1)\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-(n+1)\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(276)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E277"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E277.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(n+1)\left\lVert({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}}){\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\Big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})-(n+1)\Big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\cdot\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(n+1)\left\lVert({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}}){\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\Big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})-(n+1)\Big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\cdot\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(277)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E278"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E278.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\cdot\sigma^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\cdot\sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(278)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the maximum eigenvalue of <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the inequality follows from the Rayleigh-Ritz theorem.
Furthermore as <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}</annotation></semantics></math> is given in (<a href="#A1.E206" title="Equation 206 ‣ Corollary A.7 (Optimal Parameters of Pretrained Models; Corollary of Theorem 1 in ( ) ). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">206</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E279"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E279.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{D}}={\mathbf{U}}\diag\left(a_{i}\right)_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{D}}={\mathbf{U}}\diag\left(a_{i}\right)_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E279.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{ where }a_{i}:=\frac{m\lambda_{i}}{(m+1)\lambda_{i}+\tr({\mathbf{\Sigma}})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{ where }a_{i}:=\frac{m\lambda_{i}}{(m+1)\lambda_{i}+\tr({\mathbf{\Sigma}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(279)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})=\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})=\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\max_{i\in[d]}(1-a_{i})^{2}=(1-a_{d})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\max_{i\in[d]}(1-a_{i})^{2}=(1-a_{d})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing with respect to <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> be sufficiently large such that <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E280"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E280.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E280.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\cdot\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\cdot\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(280)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">holds from the Rayleigh-Ritz theorem. Therefore, if <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E281"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E281.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E281.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\sigma^{2}=-(n+1)a_{d}(2-a_{d})\lambda_{1}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}\|_{2}^{2}+\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}\big(\lambda_{1}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}\|_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})+(n+1)(\delta-1)\big)\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\sigma^{2}=-(n+1)a_{d}(2-a_{d})\lambda_{1}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}\|_{2}^{2}+\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}\big(\lambda_{1}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}\|_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(281)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is equal to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E282"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E282.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E282.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}\cdot\frac{\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}}{a_{d}(2-a_{d})\cdot\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}}-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i\in[d]}a_{i}^{2}\cdot\frac{\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}}{a_{d}(2-a_{d})\cdot\lambda_{1}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}}-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(282)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">then it follows <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})\cdot\sigma^{2}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A1.E278" title="Equation 278 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">278</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E280" title="Equation 280 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">280</span></a>). Therefore, condition (<a href="#A1.E271" title="Equation 271 ‣ Corollary A.14 (Test Error of Pretrained Models). ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">271</span></a>) also holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, because <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy (<a href="#A1.E206" title="Equation 206 ‣ Corollary A.7 (Optimal Parameters of Pretrained Models; Corollary of Theorem 1 in ( ) ). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">206</span></a>), it follows from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2 Proofs of Statistical Properties of Model Outputs ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E283"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E283.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E283.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}({\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2})+\frac{n}{n+1}{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}({\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2})+\frac{n}{n+1}{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(283)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E284"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E284.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{n}{n+1}2{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+n+2)({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{n}{n+1}2{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}(\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})+n+2)({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(284)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E285"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E285.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(285)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E286"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E286.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\frac{n}{n+1}{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-2)a_{i}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\frac{n}{n+1}{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-2)a_{i}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(286)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is monotone decreasing in <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{i}-2)a_{i}\lambda_{i}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{i}-2)a_{i}\lambda_{i}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the minimum error is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E287"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E287.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E287.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-2)a_{i}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-2)a_{i}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(287)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E288"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E288.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-1)^{2}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{U}}\diag((a_{i}-1)^{2}\lambda_{i})_{i\in[d]}{\mathbf{U}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\theta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(288)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.15</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\Sigma}}=\lambda{\mathbf{I}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\Sigma}}=\lambda{\mathbf{I}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by the parameters
in (<a href="#A1.E206" title="Equation 206 ‣ Corollary A.7 (Optimal Parameters of Pretrained Models; Corollary of Theorem 1 in ( ) ). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">206</span></a>).
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E289"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E289.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]\leq\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]\leq\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(289)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holds <em id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">if and only if</em></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E290"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E290.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\geq\frac{da}{2-a}\Bigl(1+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}}\Bigr)-1,\qquad a:=\frac{m}{m+1+d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\geq\frac{da}{2-a}\Bigl(1+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}}\Bigr)-1,\qquad a:=\frac{m}{m+1+d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(290)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the condition in (<a href="#A1.E290" title="Equation 290 ‣ Corollary A.15. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">290</span></a>) reduces to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E291"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E291.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\geq d\Bigl(1+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}}\Bigr)-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\geq d\Bigl(1+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}}\Bigr)-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(291)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\Sigma}}=\lambda{\mathbf{I}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\Sigma}}=\lambda{\mathbf{I}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, all eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> are equal and
(<a href="#A1.E206" title="Equation 206 ‣ Corollary A.7 (Optimal Parameters of Pretrained Models; Corollary of Theorem 1 in ( ) ). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">206</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E292"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E292.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{D}}:={\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}=a{\mathbf{I}}_{d},\qquad a=\frac{m}{m+1+d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{D}}:={\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}=a{\mathbf{I}}_{d},\qquad a=\frac{m}{m+1+d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(292)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})=da^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})=da^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}})^{2}=(a-1)^{2}{\mathbf{I}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}})^{2}=(a-1)^{2}{\mathbf{I}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem A.13. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>, the condition to satisfy is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E293"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E293.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E293.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{C}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(293)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E294"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E294.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(n+1)\|({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}}){\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})-(n+1)\big)\|{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(n+1)\|({\mathbf{D}}-{\mathbf{I}}){\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+\big(\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})-(n+1)\big)\|{\mathbf{\Sigma}}^{1/2}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+\tr({\mathbf{D}}^{2})\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(294)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E295"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E295.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(-(n+1)a(2-a)+da^{2}\Big)\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+da^{2}\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(-(n+1)a(2-a)+da^{2}\Big)\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+da^{2}\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(295)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E296"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E296.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n+1)a(2-a)\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}\geq da^{2}\big(\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n+1)a(2-a)\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}\geq da^{2}\big(\lambda\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(296)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is equivalent to the necessary and sufficient condition in
(<a href="#A1.E290" title="Equation 290 ‣ Corollary A.15. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">290</span></a>).
Taking <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.16</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Test Error of Fully Fine-Tuned Models)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a target task <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the family of parameters <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S4.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Optimal Parameters of Fully Fine-Tuned Models). ‣ 4.2 Fine-Tuning All Parameters with Zero-Shot Loss ‣ 4 Optimal Parameters and Test Error of Learned Linear Attention Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>). Then, for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following inequality holds:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E297"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E297.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}=\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);0,{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})&lt;\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);n,{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}=\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);0,{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})&lt;\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);n,{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(297)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the test errors are given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E298"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E298.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);0,{\mathbf{\theta}})=\sigma^{2}+({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);0,{\mathbf{\theta}})=\sigma^{2}+({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(298)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E299"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E299.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);n,{\mathbf{\theta}})=\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathcal{E}(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}(w);n,{\mathbf{\theta}})=\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(299)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2 Proofs of Statistical Properties of Model Outputs ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E300"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E300.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(300)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging in the optimal zero-shot parameters in (<a href="#A1.E215" title="Equation 215 ‣ Theorem A.8 (Optimal Parameters of Fully Fine-Tuned Models). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">215</span></a>), i.e., <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}={\mathbf{0}}_{d}{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}={\mathbf{0}}_{d}{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{v}}_{21}=c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{v}}_{21}=c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=1/c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=1/c</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E301"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E301.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E301.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}-2{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}=({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})+\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2}+{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}-2{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}=({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})+\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(301)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, under the same parameter choice, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E302"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E302.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E302.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(n+2)({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})+\frac{1}{c^{2}}\Big((c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}(c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})+\sigma^{2}\Big)-2{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(n+2)({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})+\frac{1}{c^{2}}\Big((c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}(c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})+\sigma^{2}\Big)-2{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(302)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E303"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E303.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E303.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})+\sigma^{2}\right)+\frac{n(n+2)}{(n+1)^{2}}({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}({\mathbf{\theta}}-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})+\sigma^{2}\right)+\frac{n(n+2)}{(n+1)^{2}}({\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(303)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E304"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E304.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(\frac{1}{c^{2}}\Big((c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}(c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})+\sigma^{2}\Big)-2{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(\frac{1}{c^{2}}\Big((c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}(c{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+{\mathbf{\theta}})+\sigma^{2}\Big)-2{\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(304)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite, for any <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E305"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E305.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E305.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(n{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\frac{1}{c^{2}}\Big((c+1)^{2}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2}\Big)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(n{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\frac{1}{c^{2}}\Big((c+1)^{2}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\sigma^{2}\Big)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(305)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E306"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E306.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(\left(n+\frac{(c+1)^{2}}{c^{2}}\right){\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\frac{1}{c^{2}}\sigma^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}+\frac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(\left(n+\frac{(c+1)^{2}}{c^{2}}\right){\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}+\frac{1}{c^{2}}\sigma^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(306)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E307"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E307.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left\lVert\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\right\rVert_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left\lVert\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\right\rVert_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(307)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, taking the limit <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E304" title="Equation 304 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">304</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E308"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E308.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]={\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]={\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{\theta}}+\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(308)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.17</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a target task <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the family of parameters <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Theorem 4.6 (Optimal Parameters and Test Error of Value-Matrix Fine-Tuned Models). ‣ 4.3 Fine-Tuning Value Matrix with Zero-Shot Loss ‣ 4 Optimal Parameters and Test Error of Learned Linear Attention Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>). Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For simplicity, define <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(w;\theta):=\mathcal{E}\big(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};n,{\mathbf{\theta}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(w;\theta):=\mathcal{E}\big(\hat{{\mathbf{V}}}(w),\hat{{\mathbf{Q}}};n,{\mathbf{\theta}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}(\theta):=w^{\star}(n;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}(\theta):=w^{\star}(n;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the excess error is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E309"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E309.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)=\frac{n\big((n+1+d)\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta+d\sigma^{2}\big)}{(n+1)^{2}}\cdot\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)=\frac{n\big((n+1+d)\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta+d\sigma^{2}\big)}{(n+1)^{2}}\cdot\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(309)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with equality if and only if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}(\theta)=w^{\star}(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}(\theta)=w^{\star}(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta=\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta=\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then (<a href="#A1.E309" title="Equation 309 ‣ Proposition A.17. ‣ A.4 Proofs for Test Errors ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">309</span></a>) reduces to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E310"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E310.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)=\frac{n(n+3+2d)^{2}}{(n+1)^{2}(d+4)^{2}}\cdot\frac{\big(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big)^{2}}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}\cdot\big(1-\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})\big)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)=\frac{n(n+3+2d)^{2}}{(n+1)^{2}(d+4)^{2}}\cdot\frac{\big(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big)^{2}}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}\cdot\big(1-\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})\big)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(310)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E311"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E311.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(\theta,\theta_{0}):=\frac{\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}}{\sqrt{(\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta)(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0})}}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(\theta,\theta_{0}):=\frac{\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}}{\sqrt{(\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta)(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0})}}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(311)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is the cosine similarity induced by the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem17.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-inner product.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From the proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem A.10 (Task-Wise Optimal 𝑤). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>, the few-shot error is a quadratic function of <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> of the form</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E312"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E312.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w;\theta)=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(a(\theta)\,w^{2}+b(\theta)\,w\big)+\mathrm{const}(\theta)=\frac{a(\theta)}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(w^{2}-\frac{b(\theta)}{a(\theta)}\,w\right)+\mathrm{const}(\theta)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>const</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>const</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w;\theta)=\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(a(\theta)\,w^{2}+b(\theta)\,w\big)+\mathrm{const}(\theta)=\frac{a(\theta)}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(w^{2}-\frac{b(\theta)}{a(\theta)}\,w\right)+\mathrm{const}(\theta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(312)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E313"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E313.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a(\theta):=n\big((n+1+d)\,\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta+d\sigma^{2}\big),\quad b(\theta):=2n\big(\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta-(n+1)\,\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a(\theta):=n\big((n+1+d)\,\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta+d\sigma^{2}\big),\quad b(\theta):=2n\big(\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta-(n+1)\,\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(313)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(\theta)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(\theta)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w^{\star}(\theta)=-b(\theta)/(2a(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}(\theta)=-b(\theta)/(2a(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E314"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E314.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w;\theta)=\frac{a(\theta)}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(w-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}+\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(w;\theta)=\frac{a(\theta)}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(w-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}+\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(314)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E315"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E315.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta\big)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)=\frac{a(\theta)}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}=\frac{n\big((n+1+d)\,\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta+d\sigma^{2}\big)}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta\big)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)=\frac{a(\theta)}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}=\frac{n\big((n+1+d)\,\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta+d\sigma^{2}\big)}{(n+1)^{2}}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)\big)^{2}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(315)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the equality condition is <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}(\theta)=w^{\star}(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}(\theta)=w^{\star}(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now assume <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta=\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\top}\Sigma\theta=\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem A.10 (Task-Wise Optimal 𝑤). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E316"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E316.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w^{\star}(\theta_{0})-w^{\star}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E316.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\big(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta-\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big)}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}=\frac{\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big(\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})-1\big)}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\big(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta-\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big)}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}=\frac{\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big(\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})-1\big)}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(316)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E317"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E317.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta\big)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta_{0});\theta\big)-\mathcal{E}\big(w^{\star}(\theta);\theta\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E317.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n\big((n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}\big)}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(\frac{\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big(\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})-1\big)}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n\big((n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}\big)}{(n+1)^{2}}\left(\frac{\frac{n+3+2d}{d+4}\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big(\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})-1\big)}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(317)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E318"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E318.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n(n+3+2d)^{2}}{(n+1)^{2}(d+4)^{2}}\cdot\frac{\big(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big)^{2}}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}\cdot\big(1-\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})\big)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n(n+3+2d)^{2}}{(n+1)^{2}(d+4)^{2}}\cdot\frac{\big(\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}\big)^{2}}{(n+1+d)\,\theta_{0}^{\top}\Sigma\theta_{0}+d\sigma^{2}}\cdot\big(1-\rho(\theta,\theta_{0})\big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(318)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To understand the role of the auxiliary few-shot objective during fine-tuning, we analyze the test error under a structured parameterization of the linear attention model in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Transformer Architecture. ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.18</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\Sigma}}={\mathbf{I}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\Sigma}}={\mathbf{I}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the parameters <math id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Transformer Architecture. ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) take the following forms:</p>
<table id="A1.E319" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E319.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}=\begin{bmatrix}0&{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;0\\
{\mathbf{0}}_{d}&{\mathbf{0}}_{d}{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&{\mathbf{0}}_{d}\\
0&amp;\alpha\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\qquad{\mathbf{Q}}=\begin{bmatrix}\beta&{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;0\\
{\mathbf{0}}_{d}&amp;\gamma\cdot{\mathbf{I}}_{d}&{\mathbf{0}}_{d}\\
0&{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>β</mi></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;0\\
{\mathbf{0}}_{d}&amp;{\mathbf{0}}_{d}{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;{\mathbf{0}}_{d}\\
0&amp;\alpha\cdot{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\qquad{\mathbf{Q}}=\begin{bmatrix}\beta&amp;{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;0\\
{\mathbf{0}}_{d}&amp;\gamma\cdot{\mathbf{I}}_{d}&amp;{\mathbf{0}}_{d}\\
0&amp;{\mathbf{0}}_{d}^{\top}&amp;0\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(319)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta,\gamma\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta,\gamma\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.19</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem18" title="Assumption A.18. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.18</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E320"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E320.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\tfrac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\cdot\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]+\tfrac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\cdot h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\tfrac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\cdot\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y\mid{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]+\tfrac{n}{(n+1)^{2}}\cdot h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(320)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E321"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E321.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot((\beta+(d+2)\gamma)\alpha-1)^{2}+\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot 2(d+2)\gamma^{2}\alpha^{2}+\sigma^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ZS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{ZS}}({\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot((\beta+(d+2)\gamma)\alpha-1)^{2}+\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot 2(d+2)\gamma^{2}\alpha^{2}+\sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(321)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E322"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E322.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot\alpha^{2}\Big((3d+n+5)\gamma^{2}+2\beta\gamma+\beta^{2}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot\alpha^{2}\Big((3d+n+5)\gamma^{2}+2\beta\gamma+\beta^{2}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(322)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E323"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E323.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad+\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot 2\alpha\Big((2d+n+3)\gamma^{2}-(d+n+3)\gamma+\beta^{2}+\beta\gamma-\beta\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad+\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot 2\alpha\Big((2d+n+3)\gamma^{2}-(d+n+3)\gamma+\beta^{2}+\beta\gamma-\beta\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(323)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E324"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E324.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad+\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\Big((d+n+1)\gamma^{2}-2(n+1)\gamma+(n+2)+\beta^{2}\Big)+\sigma^{2}(d\gamma^{2}+n+2+\beta^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad+\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\Big((d+n+1)\gamma^{2}-2(n+1)\gamma+(n+2)+\beta^{2}\Big)+\sigma^{2}(d\gamma^{2}+n+2+\beta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(324)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1)^{2}+\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1)^{2}+\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})=d\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})=d\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})=d\gamma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tr({\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{11}{\mathbf{\Sigma}})=d\gamma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2 Proofs of Statistical Properties of Model Outputs ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, we have (<a href="#A1.E321" title="Equation 321 ‣ Lemma A.19. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">321</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E322" title="Equation 322 ‣ Lemma A.19. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">322</span></a>).
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E325"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E325.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E325.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0+\lim_{n\to\infty}\tfrac{1}{n}\cdot h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1)^{2}+\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0+\lim_{n\to\infty}\tfrac{1}{n}\cdot h({\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}};{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0})=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1)^{2}+\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(325)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.20</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem18" title="Assumption A.18. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.18</span></a>, suppose the parameters are close to the optimal zero-shot solution in Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem A.8 (Optimal Parameters of Fully Fine-Tuned Models). ‣ A.3 Proofs for Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>. If one additional gradient descent step is performed on the asymptotic few-shot prompt loss in (<a href="#S4.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ 4.4 Fine-Tuning Value Matrix with Zero-Shot and Auxiliary Few-Shot Losses ‣ 4 Optimal Parameters and Test Error of Learned Linear Attention Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) with a sufficiently small learning rate <math id="A1.Thmtheorem20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then the zero-shot error increases.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">From (<a href="#A1.E321" title="Equation 321 ‣ Lemma A.19. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">321</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem19" title="Lemma A.19. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.19</span></a>, define the zero-shot error as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E326"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E326.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E326.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\big((\beta+(d+2)\gamma)\alpha-1\big)^{2}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+2(d+2)\alpha^{2}\gamma^{2}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\big((\beta+(d+2)\gamma)\alpha-1\big)^{2}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+2(d+2)\alpha^{2}\gamma^{2}\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}+\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(326)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem19" title="Lemma A.19. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.19</span></a>, the asymptotic few-shot loss under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem18" title="Assumption A.18. ‣ A.5 Proofs for Test Errors under the Auxiliary Few-Shot Prompt Loss ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.18</span></a> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E327"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E327.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\alpha,\beta,\gamma):=\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1)^{2}+\sigma^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>FS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\alpha,\beta,\gamma):=\lim_{n\to\infty}\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}},y|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}}\left[\big(\hat{y}_{\mathrm{FS}}({\mathbf{Z}}_{[n]},{\mathbf{x}};{\mathbf{V}},{\mathbf{Q}})-y\big)^{2}\right]=\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\cdot(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1)^{2}+\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(327)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">One gradient descent step with step size <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E328"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E328.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E328.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\alpha}=-2\eta\gamma\big(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2},\qquad\Delta\beta=0,\qquad\Delta\gamma=-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\gamma}=-2\eta(\alpha+1)\big(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\alpha}=-2\eta\gamma\big(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2},\qquad\Delta\beta=0,\qquad\Delta\gamma=-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\gamma}=-2\eta(\alpha+1)\big(\gamma\alpha+\gamma-1\big)\left\lVert{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(328)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">At the zero-shot optimum <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)=(1,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)=(1,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, one gradient descent step gives <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\gamma=4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\gamma=4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is updated to <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1,4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1,4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E329"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E329.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(1,1,4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2})-\mathcal{E}(1,1,0)=(d+2)(d+4)\big(4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}\big)^{2}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}=16(d+2)(d+4)\eta^{2}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{6}&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(1,1,4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2})-\mathcal{E}(1,1,0)=(d+2)(d+4)\big(4\eta\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}\big)^{2}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}=16(d+2)(d+4)\eta^{2}\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{6}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(329)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and by continuity the same holds in a neighborhood of <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional details on the experimental setup and supplementary results for the linear regression tasks in Section <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Experimental Setup and Additional Results for Linear Regression Tasks ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> and the MMLU benchmark in Section <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Experimental Setup and Additional Results for the MMLU Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Experimental Setup and Additional Results for Linear Regression Tasks</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experimental Setup.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ahn et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, we use the setup in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Problem Setup ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\Sigma}}={\mathbf{I}}_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\Sigma}}={\mathbf{I}}_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n=20</annotation></semantics></math>:
In the pretraining phase, we generate data by sampling <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{0}}_{5},{\mathbf{I}}_{5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{0}}_{5},{\mathbf{I}}_{5})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{0}}_{5},{\mathbf{I}}_{5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{0}}_{5},{\mathbf{I}}_{5})</annotation></semantics></math>, and setting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y={\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y={\mathbf{\theta}}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+e</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We fix the number of shots to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=20</annotation></semantics></math> during pretraining.
For fine-tuning, we first randomly generate a target task vector <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We then construct the fine-tuning dataset by sampling <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{0}}_{5},{\mathbf{I}}_{5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{0}}_{5},{\mathbf{I}}_{5})</annotation></semantics></math> and generating <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y={\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}+e</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>. When using the auxiliary few-shot loss during fine-tuning, we fix the number of shots to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Experiments on Linear Regression Tasks ‣ 5 Empirical Validation ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> reports results for the linear self-attention model in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Transformer Architecture. ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), which uses a merged query–key matrix.
In additional experiments, we also consider a variant with separate query and key matrices, following the standard attention formulation, as well as a 2-head attention model. All of these variants exhibit similar trends.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Additional Results.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-shot test errors on the in-distribution task <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the out-of-distribution task <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> across fine-tuning strategies. Empty circles denote models fine-tuned with the zero-shot (ZS) loss only, whereas filled circles denote models fine-tuned with both the zero-shot and few-shot (FS) losses. Parentheses indicate which parameters are updated: <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">all</span> updates all parameters, while <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">K</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Q</span>, and <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">V</span> update the key, query, and value matrices, respectively. Value-matrix fine-tuning without the auxiliary few-shot loss achieves the lowest 20-shot error on the out-of-distribution task <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23197v1/linear_h1_thetas.svg" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:267/145;" width="267" height="145"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.F7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Test errors on <span id="A2.F7.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Left) </span>the in-distribution task <math id="A2.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="A2.F7.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Right) </span>the out-of-distribution task <math id="A2.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, using a 1-head attention model.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23197v1/linear_h2_thetas.svg" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:267/145;" width="267" height="145"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Test errors on <span id="A2.F8.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Left) </span>the in-distribution task <math id="A2.F8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="A2.F8.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Right) </span>the out-of-distribution task <math id="A2.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\mathbf{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, using a 2-head attention model.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Experimental Setup and Additional Results for the MMLU Benchmark</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experimental Setup.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the LLaMAFactory framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2024</a>)</cite> for all experiments. All runs are conducted on a single NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPU or NVIDIA RTX A5000 GPU.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> on the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> subset of MMLU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, which contains 1,000 training examples. For each fine-tuning instance, we use <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-4.1-mini</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Achiam et al., 2023</a>)</cite> to generate a chain-of-thought rationale, and train the model on prompts that include both the final answer and the reasoning trace. Fine-tuning is performed for 5 epochs using low-rank adaptation (LoRA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2022</a>)</cite> with rank <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=128</annotation></semantics></math>. We apply adapters either to all attention projection matrices or only to the query (Q), key (K), and value (V) projections. We adopt LoRA as a parameter-efficient approach for optimizing the zero-shot objective (ZS), which is also theoretically motivated by our analysis where the optimal parameter change admits a rank-one update under value-matrix fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We sweep the learning rate over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1\times 10^{-3},3\times 10^{-4},1\times 10^{-4},3\times 10^{-5},1\times 10^{-5}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1\times 10^{-3},3\times 10^{-4},1\times 10^{-4},3\times 10^{-5},1\times 10^{-5}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and select the model that achieves the best zero-shot performance on the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> category. When using the zero-shot objective with the auxiliary few-shot objective (ZS+FS), we sweep the initial weight of the few-shot loss term over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.25,0.50,0.75,1.00\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.75</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.00</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.25,0.50,0.75,1.00\}</annotation></semantics></math> and linearly anneal it to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> within each epoch. We evaluate the resulting models on the MMLU test set across four categories (<em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em>, <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Social Sciences</em>, <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STEM</em>, and <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Other</em>), consisting of 1,000 examples in total. Inference is performed with a temperature of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, evaluation is repeated three times, and the mean accuracy is reported along with the standard error.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Additional Results.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our fine-tuning objective is primarily to improve performance on the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> category. Therefore, the models trained with <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS fine-tuning on Q/K/V</em>, <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS fine-tuning on V</em>, and <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS+FS fine-tuning on V</em> achieve substantial zero-shot improvements on <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em>, with gains of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+5.69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5.69</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+5.69</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.59" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.59</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.59</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.00</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points (pp), respectively, whereas <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS fine-tuning on Q</em> and <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS fine-tuning on K</em> yield considerably smaller gains (<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+2.44" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2.44</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+2.44</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+2.81" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2.81</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+2.81</annotation></semantics></math> pp). In the remainder, we therefore focus on the three competitive variants.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These trends change in the 7-shot setting. In particular, <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS fine-tuning on Q/K/V</em> substantially harms few-shot performance, reducing 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> accuracy by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-4.07" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4.07</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-4.07</annotation></semantics></math> pp and 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STEM</em> accuracy by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-5.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-5.05</annotation></semantics></math> pp. In contrast, <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS fine-tuning on V</em> better preserves few-shot generalization, with only a <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.38" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.38</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.38</annotation></semantics></math> pp change on 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> and a <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.42</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.42</annotation></semantics></math> pp change on 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STEM</em>. Moreover, incorporating the auxiliary few-shot objective (<em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ZS+FS fine-tuning on V</em>) further improves few-shot performance on categories closer to the fine-tuning domain: it increases 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Social Sciences</em> by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.23" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.23</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.23</annotation></semantics></math> pp and reduces the 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> drop to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1.77" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.77</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1.77</annotation></semantics></math> pp (compared to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.38" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.38</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.38</annotation></semantics></math> pp without the auxiliary loss). However, this auxiliary objective comes at a clear cost on <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STEM</em>, where it decreases 7-shot <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STEM</em> accuracy by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-6.48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6.48</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-6.48</annotation></semantics></math> pp (vs. <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.42</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.42</annotation></semantics></math> pp without the auxiliary loss). Overall, these results indicate that value-matrix fine-tuning best preserves few-shot capability, while the auxiliary few-shot objective primarily improves few-shot performance on semantically similar categories but can significantly harm out-of-domain generalization. Detailed results are reported in Table <a href="#A2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Additional Results. ‣ B.2 Experimental Setup and Additional Results for the MMLU Benchmark ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and are summarized in Figure <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5.1 Experiments on Linear Regression Tasks ‣ 5 Empirical Validation ‣ Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning:A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T2.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="A2.T2.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Zero-shot and 7-shot accuracies evaluated on four MMLU categories (<em id="A2.T2.10.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em>, <em id="A2.T2.10.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Social Sciences</em>, <em id="A2.T2.10.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STEM</em>, and <em id="A2.T2.10.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Other</em>). We fine-tune the base model (<span id="A2.T2.10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct</span>) on the <em id="A2.T2.10.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Humanities</em> subset.
ZS and FS denote fine-tuning with the zero-shot objective and the auxiliary few-shot objective, respectively, and Q, K, and V indicate that LoRA adapters are applied to the query, key, and value matrices, respectively.
The second row for each model reports the difference from the base model in percentage points.
</span></figcaption>
